MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 feels useful because a screen could let me view compatible security cameras and manage home devices in one place.",
    "The Blink bundle feels like a natural extension of my existing Blink setup because a doorbell and more cameras could cover additional entry points."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD Fire TV sticks add little because I already have a 4K stick and a Fire TV television; another streaming device does not address a clear need.",
    "The tablet and extra voice-only speakers feel less compelling because I have a clearer use for camera viewing than for another general-purpose device or voice-control point."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning Fire TV and Blink devices seems to have been taken as interest in almost anything connected to Alexa.",
    "My streaming purchases seem to have been interpreted as a reason to buy more streaming sticks, even when they duplicate equipment I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What matters now is whether a device adds a useful capability, such as viewing cameras or monitoring another entrance, beyond what I already own.",
    "My interest in similar devices is conditional: I would prefer the larger Echo Show over buying both displays, and I would need a specific appliance in mind before choosing a smart plug."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized my connected-home interests but gave too much weight to shared branding and too little to what would actually extend my current setup."
}
